const double EPSILON = 1e-10;

bool isDegeneratePlane(double a, double b, double c) {
    return std::fabs(a) < EPSILON && std::fabs(b) < EPSILON && std::fabs(c) < EPSILON;
}
```

This handles edge cases like:
- User enters `0.0000000001, 0, 0, -1` (technically a nearly-perpendicular plane)
- Floating-point arithmetic producing near-zero values during intermediate calculations

